            "title": "Is the AI bubble about to burst? Think again, say these analysts",
            "description": "<p>Despite fears of an imminent crash in AI stocks, infrastructure spending is set to hit new heights in the coming years, according to analysts at firms including Citigroup and Jefferies (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JEF\">JEF</a>). Boosted by hyperscalers like Microsoft  (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSFT\">MSFT</a>), Meta (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/META\">META</a>) and Apple (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL\">AAPL</a>), AI spending could reach $2.8 Trillion by 2029. For more live coverage of markets watch the full episode of<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cLr6hc2-oMY&list=PLx28zU8ctIRqTE7Y4uXTY-S2oHlwDsL5c\"> Market Sunrise</a> and head to<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/\"> Yahoo Finance</a>.</p>",
